From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 20 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: enable hardware watchdog autostart

The A733 watchdog hardware + the sunxi_wdt driver + the DT node
watchdog@2050000 are all in place; the watchdog is not started
(WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART defaults to n on ARCH_SUNXI in
drivers/watchdog/Kconfig and the defconfig sets no WDT option; verified
against radxa-pkg/u-boot-dlan17 @ b1cec0a9 + radxa/u-boot @ 9da4b3e82d64).

Enable CONFIG_WDT / CONFIG_WDT_SUNXI / CONFIG_WATCHDOG /
CONFIG_WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART so U-Boot starts the 16s watchdog
(CONFIG_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT_MSECS default 16000 for ARCH_SUNXI) during its
own init - protects against U-Boot-stage hangs during autoboot + image
load.

U-Boot has no stop-before-Linux path, and none is needed: Linux keeps a
watchdog that is running when sunxi_wdt probes. Since v6.18.53 (stable
e1daf1ef08e7, mainline aab55360fa11, "watchdog: sunxi_wdt: preserve
boot-enabled watchdog") sunxi_wdt_probe() tests WDT_MODE_EN, takes the
interval programmed in WDT_MODE (U-Boot's 16s), calls sunxi_wdt_start()
(programs that interval, selects the system-reset mode, sets WDT_MODE_EN)
and sets WDOG_HW_RUNNING before it registers the device
(drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c:322-331 at v6.18.54). The watchdog core
then pings it until userspace first opens /dev/watchdog (systemd
RuntimeWatchdogSec), for as long as watchdog.open_timeout allows. A
watchdog that is not running at probe is left alone. Up to v6.18.52 the
probe called sunxi_wdt_stop() unconditionally (sunxi_wdt.c:289 at
v6.18.52), so with such a kernel the watchdog U-Boot started would be
stopped at probe and stay off until userspace opens the device.

Observed on an A733 board with a kernel that has that change (the watchdog
armed by U-Boot, nothing opening /dev/watchdog): WDT_MODE reads 0xB1
(interval 0b1011 = 16s, enable set) at 14, 34 and 99 s of uptime.

REQUIREMENT at the kernel layer: the kernel must
build CONFIG_SUNXI_WATCHDOG=y (built-in, not a module), so that the probe
takes the watchdog over within the 16s that remain after U-Boot's last
service of it, before the root mount and udev.

Which of the SoC's watchdogs U-Boot arms is decided by
sunxi-cubie-a7s-watchdog-on-wdt-cpus, which moves it from WDT0 to WDT_CPUS.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
index c145d3381c2..d0e7e6c59ce 100644
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
@@ -76,3 +76,7 @@ CONFIG_SCSI_AHCI=y
 CONFIG_SPI=y
 CONFIG_UFS=y
 CONFIG_UFS_SUNXI=y
+CONFIG_WDT=y
+CONFIG_WDT_SUNXI=y
+CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
+CONFIG_WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART=y
